Task: Verify the inbound-email handler persists the new fields (Phase 1.5, Tier 2)

WHAT CHANGED
app/api/inbound-email/handler.ts — the rental_payments insert now writes
management_fees, letting_fees, lease_fees, sundry_fees, other_outgoings,
net_received, extracted and confidence, and sets fees_confirmed_at explicitly
to null.

Added scripts/verify-rental-statement-ingest.ts plus an npm alias
`verify:rent-ingest`.

Files:
  app/api/inbound-email/handler.ts (modified)
  scripts/verify-rental-statement-ingest.ts (new)
  package.json (modified)

THE CORE WHY
The parser now returns gross rent and a fee breakdown; without this the extra
fields were parsed and discarded, and the agent-fee deduction would still have
come from the management_fee_pct estimate even for statements the system had
already read.

fees_confirmed_at is set to null EXPLICITLY rather than left to the column
default, with a comment, because it is a deliberate decision and not an
oversight: an extraction is a model's proposal, so ingested fees are not
claimable until a human accepts them. This is the same gate
loan_statements.confirmed_at applies to interest.

`amount` carries an inline comment recording that it is gross rent and what
went wrong when it was not, because that is the line a future change is most
likely to get wrong again.

DELIBERATELY NOT DONE
The statement PDF attached to the email is not stored to statement_path. The
expense branch does store its primary attachment, so the asymmetry is
intentional: spec "Out of scope" lists inbound-email auto-attachment of
statement PDFs. Doing it here would have been easy and unsanctioned.

